                                <pre><h1>             Exercise Name: Bicycle Crunches.</h1></pre>
 

<b><u>Video Overview:</u></b>
    The 3D anatomical animation shows a model lying flat on an exercise mat, performing alternating pedal movements<br><br> with the legs while bringing opposite elbows toward opposite knees. The entire abdominal wall, including the rectus<br><br> abdominis and obliques, is highlighted in red and yellow to demonstrate target muscle activation during rotation and<br><br> leg extensions.

</div>
</div>


<pre>
<h1> Step-by-Step How to Perform</h1>

<u><b><h4>1.Starting Position:</h4></b></u> Lie flat on your back on an exercise mat. Place your hands lightly behind your head (without pulling on your neck), lift your legs off the floor, and bend your knees at a 90-degree angle.
<u><b><h4>2.Set the Core:</h4></b></u> Press your lower back flat against the floor by pulling your belly button in toward your spine.
<u><b><h4>3.Execute the Movement:</h4></b></u>
 Exhale and lift your head, neck, and shoulder blades slightly off the mat.
 Twist your upper body to bring yourright elbow toward your left knee while simultaneously extending yourright leg straight out at a 45-degree angle.


<u><b><h4>4.Switch Sides: </h4></b></u>Inhale as you transition, then exhale and twist to bring yourleft elbow toward your right knee while extending yourleft leg.
<u><b><h4>5.Continuous Rhythm:</h4></b></u> Continue alternating sides in a smooth, controlled pedaling motion without letting your heels touch the floor.

---

<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

<b>◉Full Core Engagement:</b> Consistently rated as one of the most effective exercises for targeting both the main six-pack muscle (rectus abdominis) and side waist (obliques) simultaneously.
<b>◉Rotational Power & Flexibility:</b> Combines flexion with rotational torso movement, enhancing dynamic abdominal strength.
<b>◉Hip Flexor Strength: </b>Strengthens the iliopsoas and lower abdominals through controlled leg lifting and extension.
<b>◉No Equipment Required:</b> A high-efficiency bodyweight exercise that builds core endurance anywhere.



<h1>Reps, Sets & Recommendations</h1>

Count1 rep every time you touch an elbow to the opposite knee on both sides (Left + Right = 1 Rep).

| Level | Reps Per Set | Sets | Rest Period |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
|Beginner | 10 – 12 reps | 3 Sets | 45 – 60 seconds |
|Intermediate | 15 – 20 reps | 3 – 4 Sets | 45 seconds |
|Advanced | 20 – 25+ reps | 4 Sets | 30 – 45 seconds |

